WEBVTT

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.190
To decide who will advance
to the Masters Tournament,

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:09.700
Satoshi will have a Promotion Match
against Kibana, ranked 8th.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.280
And today,
that battle is finally at hand.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:18.000
Knuckle City, Galar Region

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.830
Aren’t you excited,
Pikachu? Lucario?

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.960
I was wondering who it was.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.340
If it isn’t my challenger for today.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.090
Huh?! Mr. Kibana?

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.300
So, why are you here so early?

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:32.760
Guess I just couldn’t sit still.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.010
What about you, Mr. Kibana?

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.310
This place is my home turf.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:39.350
Am I not supposed to be here?

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:43.610
Man, I never thought
you’d make it up this far.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.030
But this is as far as you get!

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:47.740
I’m winning this.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.530
I didn’t come here to lose!

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:55.620
Mornin’, Satoshi, Kibana.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.080
Mr. Dande!

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.120
What were you doing,
sleeping there?

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:00.790
Well...

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:04.090
I didn’t want to be late
for your battle.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:05.960
Guess I got here
too early instead!

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.340
You, too? Really?

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:11.430
I’m gonna win the battle today for sure,
and then I’ll battle you, Mr. Dande!

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.800
Yeah.
I’m looking forward to it.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.890
You hear that, Pikachu?!

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.770
Now, show me a battle
that can’t be topped!

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:07.790
Let’s put our all
into cheering for him!

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:15.430
Ladies and gentlemen...

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:20.760
The world’s greatest Pokémon battles:
the Pokémon World Championships.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.680
The title conferred upon
the top-ranked eight: the Masters Eight.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:30.150
With that title on the line,
the final Promotion Match of the season will now begin.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:33.860
First up, and currently ranked 9th...

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:35.860
His battles are impossible to predict.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:40.830
From the moment he entered the Championships,
he raced his way up here in the blink of an eye.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.620
Competitor Satoshi,
from Kanto!

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.580
Satoshi!

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:49.710
And his opponent...

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:53.380
Currently ranked 8th,
the Gym Leader of our Knuckle City.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:58.840
The Dragon Storm who conquers battles
with his passionate heart and cool-headed tactics...

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.600
Competitor Kibana!

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:07.640
Mr. Kibana sure has a lot of fans...

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.770
R-Right.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.520
We can’t be outdone!

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.780
Satoshi! You can do it!

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:20.910
This match will decide
who advances to the Masters Tournament...

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.200
What sort of battle will we witness?
You must be excited, right, Champion?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.540
The stadium is oozing
with their ardent fighting spirit.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.290
This is going to be
an incredibly fun battle!

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:35.760
This match will use
the Masters Tournament Regulations.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.670
You may each use three Pokémon.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:41.140
There is no limit on match length
or switching out Pokémon.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:46.600
Whoever makes all three of their opponent’s Pokémon
unable to battle will be the winner.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:53.270
Additionally, you are allowed a single use of only one
of the following: Daimax, Mega Evolution, or a Z-Move.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:57.780
So Satoshi’s planning
to Mega Evolve Lucario, huh?

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:01.780
Now then, both battlers,
send your first Pokémon out onto the field!

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:02.570
Three!

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:03.490
Two!

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:04.410
One!

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:05.540
Go!

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:06.490
Here we go!

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:06.490
I choose you!

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:15.630
A Dragon showdown!

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.630
Competitor Satoshi’s first choice is Kairyu,
and Competitor Kibana’s is Flygon!

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:23.140
Let the battle begin!

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:24.510
Dragon Claw!

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.640
Dragon Dance!

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:31.980
Steel Wings!

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.110
Dodge it!

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.280
Flygon launches a stunningly fast
barrage of attacks!

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:42.780
Yet Kairyu has raised its Speed and Attack
with Dragon Dance...

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.490
...and dodges by the skin of its teeth!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.200
Your Kairyu’s real impressive.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.370
You’ve trained it well.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.370
Happy to hear that from you,
Mr. Kibana!

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:52.420
Aren’t you happy too, Kairyu?

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.630
But don’t think you can best me
when it comes to Dragon types.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:01.510
Let the winds blow!
Stream forward, Sandstorm!

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:13.270
Sandstorm...
This isn’t good.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:17.270
Kairyu’s going to keep taking damage
in that storm!

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.940
Kairyu, calm down!

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.740
Dragon Claw!

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.160
Kairyu!

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.160
Steel Wings!

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:38.170
Kairyu is at the mercy
of the elusive Flygon!

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.670
What will
Competitor Satoshi do now?!

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.670
Kairyu, can you keep going?

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.930
Okay! If we can’t find it,
we’ll just do this till we hit it...

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.690
Kairyu! Use Draco Meteor!

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.830
There! Hurricane!

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:15.920
Found it!

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:16.920
Dragon Claw!

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:23.550
Kairyu catches it!

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.220
Flygon!

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:31.680
But Flygon immediately gets back up
and vanishes back into the sandstorm!

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.680
Again?!

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:38.190
Kairyu!
Use Draco Meteor again!

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.230
I won’t fall for that twice!

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.400
Steel Wings!

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:50.740
Kairyu is unable to battle!

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:58.460
Competitor Kibana
is as tough as you’d expect!

00:07:58.460 --> 00:08:01.250
The Masters Eight
are a nigh-insurmountable wall!

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:04.340
Kibana’s a trainer whose hunger
for victory surpasses all others’.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:08.130
That makes my battles with him
all the more thrilling!

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:14.720
Kairyu, you take a nice rest.

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:16.640
Gänger...

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:17.890
I’m counting on you!

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:24.730
Competitor Satoshi’s
second Pokémon is Gänger!

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:29.200
No matter what he picks,
no one can escape from my Sandstorm!

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:30.570
Steel Wings!

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.870
Gänger, dodge it!

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:36.500
Ice Punch!

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.290
Dragon Claw!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.170
Flygon is toying with Gänger!

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:52.680
If I can’t do something
about this sandstorm...

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:55.680
He’s completely helpless...

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.850
It’s over for you!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:08:59.940
Crunch!

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.570
Gänger!

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:16.740
Crunch! It’s super effective!

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.350
Gänger is down and not moving!

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:45.520
If he loses Gänger,
Satoshi only has one Pokémon left.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.820
Mr. Kibana’s still unharmed.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:51.030
Satoshi’s at an overwhelming
disadvantage!

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.990
Can you keep going, Gänger?

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:00.120
Somehow,
it managed to stand back up!

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:05.080
That’s the trainer who fascinated Dande
for you, huh?

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:07.880
You said you wanted to battle Dande,
didn’t you?

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:10.050
The Champion you so admire.

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:13.180
But that’s not gonna be enough!

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:16.220
What’s your reason
for wanting to battle Dande?

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.140
It’s gotta be to win!

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:21.600
I’m not gonna lose
to admiration without backbone!

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:24.480
I’ll topple you,
and I’ll topple Dande!

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:27.150
<i>I’m</i> gonna be the Champion!

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:30.940
That’s right. I...

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:34.200
...admire Mr. Dande,
and I’ve wanted to battle him for ages!

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.740
But that’s not all!

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.030
I wanna beat Mr. Dande!

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.870
That’s why I can’t lose here!

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.050
Sorry, Lucario.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:53.050
I’ll Mega Evolve you next time!

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:59.640
Let’s go, Gänger!

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:05.270
Huh?!
He couldn’t be about to...?!

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.770
Let’s get huge!

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.570
Kyodaimax!

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:31.170
Whoa, Competitor Satoshi’s Gänger
has Kyodaimaxed!

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:34.340
Gänger!
Suck up the Sandstorm!

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:45.890
Kyodai Phantom!

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:54.780
Crunch!

00:11:57.910 --> 00:11:58.820
Dai Fairy!

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.800
Flygon is unable to battle!

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:27.690
Competitor Satoshi pulls Gänger
out of a crisis using his wits!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.810
Wow! Satoshi!

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.610
We did it, Gänger!

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:38.360
You did well, Flygon.

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:39.910
You’re up next...

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:41.160
Numelgon!

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:48.160
Competitor Kibana’s
second Pokémon is Numelgon!

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:52.790
I’ll show you the reason
they call me the Dragon Storm.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.550
Numelgon!
Use Rain Prayer!

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.180
Now rain, too?

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:09.440
His strategy of controlling the weather
to steer the battle in his favor...

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:12.440
This is Competitor Kibana
at his best!

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:16.690
When you’re all heated up,
the cold rain really soaks into your skin...

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.190
Numelgon, use Thunder!

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:23.700
Gänger!

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:24.990
Surf!

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.580
Hydro Pump!

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:35.460
Kyodaimax Gänger
has no way to fight back!

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:39.510
Gänger!

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:44.550
Okay... Got it.

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:48.140
What’s wrong?
Not gonna switch?

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.850
Then I’ll take the invitation to defeat it!

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.100
Surf!

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:01.820
What’s this?!
It brushed away the Surf!

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:03.820
Great work, Gänger!

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:06.370
Gänger!

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.500
Yeah! We’re gonna win!

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.540
Go for it! Dai Fairy!

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:14.460
Hydro Pump!

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:41.860
Numelgon and Gänger
are both unable to battle!

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:46.370
Both went down at the same time!
Even the effect of Rain Prayer has vanished!

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:48.450
Thank you, Gänger.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.910
Have a good, long break,
Numelgon.

00:14:56.250 --> 00:15:01.260
Satoshi and Mr. Kibana...
Their next Pokémon are their last ones!

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.170
I’m counting on you, Lucario!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.170
Here we go, Duraludon!

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:08.390
Competitor Satoshi’s
third Pokémon is Lucario.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:12.890
Competitor Kibana goes for his
absolute ace, Duraludon.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:18.400
And Competitor Kibana
still has his trump card of Daimax.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.900
We’re not giving up
till it’s over!

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:22.940
We’re gonna win this!

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:28.870
Awesome fighting spirit...
I can tell you’re serious!

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:33.370
And that’s why I’ll go all out to beat...
and crush you!

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.160
Duraludon!

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.580
What?! Already?!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:42.300
Bring the storm!
My partner!

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.590
Blow the whole stadium away!

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:46.430
Kyodaimax!

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:54.680
There’s Duraludon’s Kyodaimax!

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:00.520
Let’s go, Lucario!
Shadow Clones!

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.040
Aura Sphere!

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:24.000
One more Aura Sphere!

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:29.640
Dai Steel!

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:35.020
Dodge it!

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.060
Lucario!

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:45.820
You’ve fought well
to make it this far.

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:46.940
But...

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.700
This is where it ends!

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:50.320
Roar, my dragon!

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:52.780
Time for my ultimate attack...
Kyodai Decay!

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:04.960
Lucario!

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:13.430
No...

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:15.350
I can’t let it end here...

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:17.060
Don’t you agree, Lucario?

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:41.250
What is that...?

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:43.880
This is what he trained
with Gekkouga...

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:49.630
No...

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:51.470
It’s even bigger!

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.170
I can feel it...

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:28.750
Our Aura...

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.380
Linking everything...

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:44.810
Lucario! Kyodai Aura Sphere!

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:48.150
Duraludon! Dai Rock!

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.990
Let’s go!

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:19.180
Duraludon is unable to battle!

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:22.430
As such,
the winner is Competitor Satoshi!

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:24.560
We did it!

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.980
Lucario, we did it!

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:34.530
Lucario topples the Kyodaimax Duraludon
with a supremely gigantic Aura Sphere!

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:37.240
He won...

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:41.160
Satoshi!

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:43.750
Satoshi... Kibana...

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:47.040
Thank you for showing me a battle
that couldn’t be topped!

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:50.750
You did your best, Duraludon.

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:01.640
I lost.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:04.600
Thank you, Mr. Kibana!

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.560
Oh, I know.
Got a moment?

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:07.190
Huh?

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.360
C’mon, smile!

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:16.780
I’ll be the one to topple you,
and Dande.

00:20:16.780 --> 00:20:17.900
So...

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:21.280
You better not lose
to anyone else first.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.040
Right!

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:25.500
Attaboy.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:31.080
And so, this season’s
Promotion Matches are through.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:34.760
The Competitors advancing
to the Masters Tournament have been determined.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:41.510
First we have our winner today,
who has just risen to 8th place, Competitor Satoshi.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:42.550
In 7th...

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:45.720
The Champion of Isshu,
Competitor Iris.

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:46.730
In 6th...

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:50.810
The winner of the Kalos League
Miare Tournament, Competitor Alan.

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:51.810
In 5th...

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:54.690
The Champion of Kalos,
Competitor Carne.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:55.900
In 4th...

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:59.740
The Champion of Kanto and Johto,
Competitor Wataru.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:00.700
In 3rd...

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:03.830
The Champion of Hoenn,
Competitor Daigo.

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:04.660
In 2nd...

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.580
The Champion of Sinnoh,
Competitor Shirona.

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:10.370
And, ranked 1st...

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:14.880
The undefeated, unbeatable Champion,
Competitor Dande!

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:19.510
The dream tourney
where these mighty eight will compete...

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:21.470
...the Masters Tournament...

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:24.140
...is nearly here!

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:34.060
Emerging victorious in his fierce battle with Kibana,
Satoshi advances to the Masters Tournament.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:40.280
From here on, he will partake in
heated matches against even stronger foes!

00:23:07.120 --> 00:23:09.530
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:10.830
Go!

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:13.290
This time,
your mission is survival.

00:23:13.710 --> 00:23:17.420
Have Pokémon battles with the other Challengers
and come out on top.

00:23:17.420 --> 00:23:19.210
You’ve got this, Go!

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:21.590
So this is Sea Kinsetsu...

00:23:21.590 --> 00:23:23.800
There were <i>this</i> many Challengers?!

00:23:23.800 --> 00:23:24.880
Go!

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:26.180
Tokio?!

00:23:26.180 --> 00:23:29.850
Watch out,
we have plenty of strong rivals.

00:23:29.850 --> 00:23:31.680
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:34.140
The Battle Royal of Betrayal!
